# Line endings are LF in the repository and in the working tree, on every OS.
# Without this the repo is at the mercy of each clone's core.autocrlf: on a
# Windows checkout with autocrlf=true every file is CRLF on disk, and any tool
# that writes LF (prettier, gofmt, an editor) makes git warn about the whole
# file — noise that hides the real diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shells still get CRLF; a .ps1 with lone LF runs, but the error
# messages of a broken one point at the wrong line.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.db binary
*.epub binary
*.exe binary
